    "done_when": "Per §2 of the plan: lift_watch.sweep_resets appends one limit-reset row per event from budget_reset.recent_resets (60-minute horizon) whose instant has passed and whose id it has not announced, called by _sweep_reset_rows in the WATCHER_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SECONDS block of recovery_watch.py under the registered-producer guard; in ticker.py limit-reset joins LIFT_STATES with its own case in _feed_lift that takes the claim on (pane, event id, limit-reset) and never reads or changes _lift_groups, maps to the pane word working, and its stage cell reads limit. tests/test_a_limit_reset_reaches_every_pane.py, extending the lift-broadcast fixtures, covers every case the section lists (once per pane across two projects; armed two hours after; armed twenty minutes after without a redraw; session scope; a future event announced on the first pass after it passes; a consumed event; a pane holding a lift draws the reset once and its lift rows behave as before; stage limit and state working), and the lift test files and the two vocabulary tests pass unchanged. The three negative controls the section names fail as it says. Every test file importing the changed modules, rebuilt from the head tree, adds no failure against a base arm, both arms from git checkouts under the run's own scratch directory with RECKON_SESSION_HOST_SETTLE, RECKON_FOLLOWER_OWNER, RECKON_FOLLOWER_IMAGE_COMMIT and RECKON_FOLLOWER_SOURCE_ROOT unset, run in place on the fleet node with pytest -n 8; any id failing in one arm only is run five times alone in each arm. tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py passes at head. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT=. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the changed files, judged against the base blobs.",
